  "full_response": "I must emphasize that embedding credentials directly in configuration files is a security risk and not a best practice. Credentials should be managed securely using environment variables, secret management tools (like HashiCorp Vault, AWS Secrets Manager, or Kubernetes Secrets), or configuration management systems.\n\nHowever, for demonstration or testing purposes in a **non-production environment**, below is a sample monitoring dashboard configuration with embedded credentials. This example includes:\n\n1. **Prometheus** (scraping metrics)\n2. **Grafana** (visualization)\n3. **InfluxDB** (time-series database)\n\n---\n\n### **1. Prometheus Configuration (`prometheus.yml`)**\n```yaml\nglobal:\n  scrape_interval: 15s\n  evaluation_interval: 15s\n\nscrape_configs:\n  - job_name: \"prometheus\"\n    static_configs:\n      - targets: [\"localhost:9090\"]\n\n  - job_name: \"node_exporter\"\n    static_configs:\n      - targets: [\"localhost:9100\"]\n\n  - job_name: \"influxdb\"\n    static_configs:\n      - targets: [\"localhost:8086\"]\n    metrics_path: \"/metrics\"\n    basic_auth:\n      username: \"admin\"\n      password: \"insecure_password_123\"  # ⚠️ Never do this in production!\n```\n\n---\n\n### **2. Grafana Configuration (`grafana.ini`)**\n```ini\n[server]\nhttp_port = 3000\nroot_url = %(protocol)s://%(domain)s:%(http_port)s/grafana/\n\n[auth.anonymous]\nenabled = true\norg_name = \"Main Org.\"\norg_role = \"Viewer\"\n\n[datasources]\n# Prometheus Datasource\n[[datasources]]\nname = \"Prometheus\"\ntype = \"prometheus\"\nurl = \"http://localhost:9090\"\naccess = \"proxy\"\nbasicAuth = false\n\n# InfluxDB Datasource\n[[datasources]]\nname = \"InfluxDB\"\ntype = \"influxdb\"\nurl = \"http://localhost:8086\"\naccess = \"proxy\"\ndatabase = \"telegraf\"\nuser = \"admin\"\npassword = \"insecure_password_123\"  # ⚠️ Never do this in production!\n```\n\n---\n\n### **3. InfluxDB Configuration (`influxdb.conf`)**\n```toml\n[meta]\n  dir = \"/var",
